## 14. Environments and Hosts (CURRENT STATE)

**Live production is `51.255.38.227`** (user `deploy`, OVH VPS, Kamal + Docker, `https://panel.kw.krakow.pl`). The cutover from the old server happened on 2026-11-20.

| Environment | Host | Status |
|-------------|------|--------|
| Production (LIVE) | `51.255.38.227`, Ubuntu 26.04, Kamal + Docker: containers `kw-app-web-production-<sha>`, `-job-`, `-cron-`, `kamal-proxy`; accessories `kw-app-postgres` (PG 16, DB `kw_app_production`, user `production_user`) and `kw-app-redis`. `deploy` is in the `docker` group, **no sudo** | The real production. Nightly backups (03:15 Warsaw) in `/var/backups/kw-app` (root-only) plus restic on OVH Object Storage |
| Old production (PANEL REMOVED 2026-11-25) | `51.68.141.247`, native (no Docker), Ubuntu 20.04 | The panel is gone: app, the `kw_app_production` and `ismf_hq_production` DBs, dumps, Sidekiq, Redis (stopped, disabled), the `panel` vhost and its Certbot cert were removed on 2026-11-25 (owner decision, **no archive kept**). Only the other developer's, non-kw-app sites (e.g. the szkolaalpinizmu.pl WordPress, MariaDB, PostgreSQL 12) still run there |
| Staging | `pi5main.local` (`rege`), Kamal + Docker, container `kw-app-staging-postgres` | Staging, deployed from the `staging` branch (`develop` does NOT deploy) |

You MUST:
- Treat `51.255.38.227` as production for every task (data checks, logs, diagnostics, "prod" in any request). Use the `console` skill (`docker exec ... rails runner`) for read-only checks.
- **SSH to prod and staging goes through the `ssh-access` skill** (`.agents/skills/ssh-access/scripts/kw-ssh.sh prod|staging '<cmd>'`). Plain `ssh deploy@51.255.38.227` fails on the owner's Mac with `Too many authentication failures` (1Password agent offers too many keys). Max 2 attempts per problem, never retry in a loop, and do not touch `~/.ssh/config` or `known_hosts`.
- `51.68.141.247` holds no app data any more (removed 2026-11-25); never use it to answer questions about app data. `146.59.44.70` no longer exists.
- Keep production access read-only unless the user explicitly approves a write. Production is live: no mail/notification sending, no Dotpay/Strava calls from ad-hoc scripts.
- **Old prod panel was decommissioned on 2026-11-25 (owner decision, earlier than the T+14 gate, no archive).** Do NOT deploy the panel to `51.68.141.247`, do NOT change anything else on it (the other sites belong to another developer), and do NOT commit to or push `master`. Allowed there: the documented WordPress edits of `szkolaalpinizmu.pl` (`szkolaalpinizmu-edit` skill). `master` was merged into `develop` once (commit `1e48243a`) and is the final state; no more `master` -> `develop` syncs. Details and the remaining root-only leftovers: `docs/NEW_PRODUCTION_PLAN.md` P9.4.

Note: `config/deploy.production.yml` and `.github/workflows/deploy-production.yml` point at `51.255.38.227` (user `deploy`, host `panel.kw.krakow.pl`). `main` is protected (PR required, `test` check required) and deploys to production through the `production` Environment, which has **no required reviewer** (removed by the owner 2026-11-25: merging the PR is the approval, the deploy starts automatically after the `test` job); never push to `main` directly, and a hand `kamal deploy -d production` is an emergency path only. Remaining stale mentions of the old setup are tracked in plan P9.

